---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/href';
import Widget from '../../components/DisturbanceDecoupling.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Disturbance and State Feedback Decoupling — ECE/ME 732">
  <p class="crumb"><a href={href("/interactives/")}>← Interactives</a></p>
  <h1>Disturbance and State Feedback Decoupling</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Aerodynamic drag is feedback the air supplies, and because it goes as the
    square of the speed, how strongly it acts depends on how fast you are
    going. A slope and a headwind are disturbances you could measure. This
    tool lets the controller add back each of those terms in turn, and shows
    what that does to the one number that should not move with the operating
    point: the eigenvalue.
  </p>
  <Widget />
</BaseLayout>
